Based on the search results, "AMG Sport" was an older trim designation used by Mercedes-Benz, often preceding or being equivalent to the current "AMG Line" trim. The fundamental difference highlighted is that "AMG Line" focuses on cosmetic enhancements (sportier styling, wheels, interior details) inspired by AMG models, while a full "AMG" model (like the CLS 53 or the previous CLS 63) features a high-performance engine and chassis upgrades designed for driving dynamics.

For the *most recent* versions of the CLS (post-2018 facelift), the primary trim available in markets like the UK is often just "AMG Line" or a variant like "AMG Line Night Edition Premium Plus", which bundles many features. The true performance model is the Mercedes-AMG CLS 53.

Since "AMG Sport" is not a current trim for the latest CLS, and its historical equivalent is the "AMG Line", I will provide the evaluation for the **Mercedes-Benz CLS AMG Line** again, as this is the most accurate representation of a modern CLS with AMG-inspired styling below the full AMG performance model.

